# Netlify edge redirects.
#
# Astro's SSG build can only express a redirect as an HTML page with a
# <meta http-equiv="refresh">, which the browser must download and render before
# it moves on — a visible flash. These rules make Netlify answer with a real HTTP
# redirect instead, so no redirect page is ever rendered. They also cover the
# wildcard cases the `redirects` block in astro.config.mjs cannot enumerate.
#
# The trailing "!" (force) is required wherever Astro also emits a file at that
# path: without it Netlify prefers the static file over the rule.
#
# English moved from /en/... to the site root; other locales stay prefixed (/nl/...).

/en                  /                     301!
/en/*                /:splat               301!

/blog                /articles             301!
/blog/*              /articles/:splat      301!
